 productivity channels\nCopy\n[Off-Platform Earnings](https://dashboard.nexlev.io/docs/mcp/quickstart#off-platform-earnings)\nWhat does @AliAbdaal sell outside of ads, and which brands sponsor the most finance channels?\nCopy\n[Network Research](https://dashboard.nexlev.io/docs/mcp/quickstart#network-research)\nWhich network is MrBeast signed to, and what other channels are under it?\nCopy\n[Understanding NexLev Responses](https://dashboard.nexlev.io/docs/mcp/quickstart#understanding-nexlev-responses)\nWhen you use NexLev through Claude, ChatGPT, or Claude Code CLI, you'll receive interactive widgets displaying:\nChannel data — Comprehensive metrics, performance indicators, and growth analytics\nSortable results — Click column headers to sort by different metrics\nExpandable details — View in-depth information for each result\nFiltering options — Refine results by various criteria\nPagination — Navigate through large result sets                                          open claw guide             [Quickstart](https://dashboard.nexlev.io/docs/mcp/quickstart#quickstart)\nConnect NexLev MCP to your preferred AI assistant and start analyzing YouTube channels in under 5 minutes. Choose the platform you use below.\n[Prerequisites](https://dashboard.nexlev.io/docs/mcp/quickstart#prerequisites)\nBefore you begin, make sure you have:\nActive NexLev account — Free for all users. [Upgrade to Pro](https://dashboard.nexlev.io/docs/mcp/quickstart?required_nexlev_lite_pro_access=true) for higher quota limits.\nClaudeChatGPTOpenClawHermes\n[Via OpenClaw](https://dashboard.nexlev.io/docs/mcp/quickstart#via-openclaw)\nHow it works. OpenClaw doesn't talk to NexLev directly — it routes tasks through Claude Code CLI or Codex CLI already installed on your machine via its ACP (Agent Client Protocol). The flow is: You (messaging app) → OpenClaw Gateway → Claude Code / Codex CLI → NexLev MCP tools\nPrerequisites — CLI installed & NexLev registered\nBefore setting up OpenClaw, confirm at least one CLI is installed and NexLev MCP is already registered in it — OpenClaw calls the CLI, which in turn calls NexLev.\nRegister NexLev in Claude Code CLI (if using Claude):\nclaude mcp add -s user --transport http nexlev https://prod.dashboard.nexlev.io/api/claude-mcp\nCopy\nRegister NexLev in Codex CLI (if using Codex):\ncodex mcp add nexlev --url https://prod.dashboard.nexlev.io/api/mcp\nCopy\nSee the Claude or ChatGPT tabs above for full CLI setup instructions.\nStep 1 — Install OpenClaw\nnpm install -g openclaw@latestopenclaw onboard --install-daemon\nCopy\nThis installs the Gateway daemon and walks you through pairing with your messaging channel (Telegram, Discord, WhatsApp, etc.).\nStep 2 — Install the acpx plugin\nACP sessions are powered by the acpx plugin. Install and enable it:\nopenclaw plugins install @openclaw/acpxopenclaw config set plugins.entries.acpx.enabled trueopenclaw config set plugins.allow '[\"acpx\"]'\nCopy\nThen enable ACP and set your default CLI:\nopenclaw config set acp.enabled trueopenclaw config set acp.backend acpxopenclaw config set acp.allowedAgents '[\"claude\", \"codex\"]' # Pick your default (whichever CLI you have installed):openclaw config set acp.defaultAgent claude# or:openclaw config set acp.defaultAgent codex\nCopy\nStep 3 — Register NexLev inside OpenClaw\nThe URL depends on which CLI OpenClaw will call:\n# If your default CLI is Claude Code:openclaw mcp set nexlev '{\"url\":\"https://prod.dashboard.nexlev.io/api/claude-mcp\",\"transport\":\"streamable-http\"}' # If your default CLI is Codex:openclaw mcp set nexlev '{\"url\":\"https://prod.dashboard.nexlev.io/api/mcp\",\"transport\":\"streamable-http\"}'\nCopy\nVerify it was saved:\nopenclaw mcp list\nCopy\nPrefer manual config? Edit ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json directly and add your server entries under mcp.servers, then run openclaw gateway restart.\nStep 4 — Authenticate NexLev\nOpenClaw inherits auth from the CLI it calls. Authenticate inside that CLI:\nclaude # or: codex/mcp# Select nexlev → Authenticate# Browser opens → log in to dashboard.nexlev.io → approve\nCopy\nSign in with the right NexLev account. If you have a paid NexLev plan (Lite, Pro, or Premium), make sure you log in with that account — your rate limits are tied to the account you connect. Signing in with a different account will apply Free plan limits instead.\nStep 5 — Spawn a session & use NexLev\nFrom your connected messaging app (Telegram, Discord, etc.), spawn a session:\n/acp spawn claude --bind here\nCopy\nThe --bind here flag pins the conversation to the session so follow-up messages route to the same CLI instance. Then just ask in natural language:\nFind 10 faceless YouTube channels in the finance niche earning over $5K/month\nCopy\nPull full analytics for @MrBeast — subscriber growth, RPM, and top videos\nCopy\nManaging the server\nTask\nCommand\nList MCP servers in OpenClaw\nopenclaw mcp list\nRemove NexLev from OpenClaw\nopenclaw mcp unset nexlev\nCheck ACP health\n/acp doctor (in chat)\nCheck active sessions\n/acp status (in chat)\nClose a session\n/acp close (in chat)\nRestart the gateway\nopenclaw gateway restart\nTroubleshooting\nNexLev tools not visible OpenClaw calls the CLI — the CLI is what talks to NexLev. Verify the CLI itself has NexLev registered: claude mcp list or codex mcp list.\nWrong endpoint Using the Claude Code URL with Codex (or vice versa) will silently fail.\nClaude Code → https://prod.dashboard.nexlev.io/api/claude-mcp\nCodex → https://prod.dashboard.nexlev.io/api/mcp\nACP spawn blocked ACP sessions run on the host runtime. If your session is sandboxed, use runtime=\"subagent\" or disable sandboxing for the session.\n[What You Can Do Next](https://dashboard.nexlev.io/docs/mcp/quickstart#what-you-can-do-next)\nOnce connected, start using NexLev tools directly inside your AI chat:\n[Long Form Channel Search](https://dashboard.nexlev.io/docs/mcp/quickstart#long-form-channel-search)\nFind 20 long-form channels related to the minecraft niche\nCopy\n[Short Form Channel Analysis](https://dashboard.nexlev.io/docs/mcp/quickstart#short-form-channel-analysis)\nShow me 15 viral YouTube Shorts channels in the comedy niche\nCopy\n[Keyword Research](https://dashboard.nexlev.io/docs/mcp/quickstart#keyword-research)\nFind high-volume, low-competition keywords for cooking content\nCopy\n[Content Strategy](https://dashboard.nexlev.io/docs/mcp/quickstart#content-strategy)\nWhat content strategy should I use for a tech review channel with 10K subscribers?\nCopy\n[Competitive Research](https://dashboard.nexlev.io/docs/mcp/quickstart#competitive-research)\nCompare successful channels in the fitness niche and identify common patterns\nCopy\n[Thumbnail Generation](https://dashboard.nexlev.io/docs/mcp/quickstart#thumbnail-generation)\nGenerate a thumbnail for my video \"I Tried Waking Up at 4AM for 30 Days\" — match the style of the top productivity channels\nCopy\n[Off-Platform Earnings](https://dashboard.nexlev.io/docs/mcp/quickstart#off-platform-earnings)\nWhat does @AliAbdaal sell outside of ads, and which brands sponsor the most finance channels?\nCopy\n[Network Research](https://dashboard.nexlev.io/docs/mcp/quickstart#network-research)\nWhich network is MrBeast signed to, and what other channels are under it?\nCopy\n[Understanding NexLev Responses](https://dashboard.nexlev.io/docs/mcp/quickstart#understanding-nexlev-responses)\nWhen you use NexLev through Claude, ChatGPT, or Claude Code CLI, you'll receive interactive widgets displaying:\nChannel data — Comprehensive metrics, performance indicators, and growth analytics\nSortable results — Click column headers to sort by different metrics\nExpandable details — View in-depth information for each result\nFiltering options — Refine results by various criteria\nPagination — Navigate through large result sets                                          now just for refreance i gave you read and understand how to do it and do if fast man \n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-08-25T23:54:36+05:30.\n\nThe user has uploaded 1 image(s):\n- C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9ecf2b20-4f14-47c7-887d-090725d6fd1c/.user_uploaded/media_1787682026991.png\nYou can embed this image in an artifact if you need the USER to review it.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
{"step_index":259,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T18:24:36Z","content":"I see it working in your Claude.ai! And I notice NexLev tools are actually **already registered** in Antigravity! Let me try calling them directly:","thinking":"Now I understand! Looking at the screenshot, the user has NexLev MCP working in Claude.ai web — it shows \"Get batch channel metrics status\" with the NexLev icon. \n\nThe key insight from the docs: ALL paths (Claude, Hermes, OpenClaw) require OAuth authentication. There's no way around it. The authentication happens through the browser OAuth flow.\n\nFor Hermes: `hermes mcp login nexlev` → browser opens → login → tokens cached at `~/.hermes/mcp-tokens/nexlev.json`\nFor OpenClaw: auth inherited from Claude Code CLI → `/mcp` → authenticate in browser\nFor Claude Code itself, the flow is similar — running `/mcp`, selecting nexlev, and authenticating opens the browser, with tokens cached for silent reuse afterward. The user already has this working in Claude.ai web, but that token lives server-side at Anthropic, not locally. Re-reading NexLev's error message, it accepts either an OAuth Bearer token or an API key passed via Authorization header, x-api-key header, or api_key query parameter — so there may be an alternate path using an API key instead of going through the full OAuth dance.\n\nNexLev's \"no API key needed\" marketing actually just refers to the OAuth flow being keyless for end users, not that API keys don't exist — the user might have one they're unaware of. For our bridge without a browser-based session, we need either the OAuth token or that API key. The real blocker has been that our Python OAuth script opens the browser fine, but the redirect back to our local callback isn't completing — the user logs in and lands on the NexLev dashboard instead of bouncing back to us, possibly because auth.nexlev.io first redirects through Google before coming back.\n\nI'm now considering