{"step_index":330,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T18:55:44Z","content":"**What I did:** Updated `mcp_config.json` to use `mcp-remote` — a Node.js proxy that runs locally via stdio and handles NexLev's OAuth automatically. No API key needed.\n\n**Config is now:**\n```json\n\"nexlev\": {\n  \"command\": \"npx\",\n  \"args\": [\"-y\", \"mcp-remote\", \"https://prod.dashboard.nexlev.io/api/claude-mcp\"]\n}\n```\n\n**What to do now:** Test it. Let me try calling a NexLev tool — `mcp-remote` will handle the OAuth:","thinking":"OK, let me recap and continue:\n\n**What I just did:**\n- Updated `mcp_config.json` to use `mcp-remote` (an npx package) as a local stdio proxy for NexLev MCP\n- The config now uses: `npx -y mcp-remote https://prod.dashboard.nexlev.io/api/claude-mcp`\n- `mcp-remote` handles OAuth automatically - it creates a local stdio server that proxies to the remote NexLev endpoint and manages the browser OAuth flow\n\n**What I need to do next:**\n- Test if the new config works by calling a NexLev tool\n- When `mcp-remote` first runs, it should open a browser for OAuth login\n- After login, it caches the token locally for reuse\n\nI should just try calling a NexLev tool now to see if the connection triggers properly. If Antigravity didn't auto-reload the MCP servers after the config change, it won't work and I'll need to tell the user to restart - but let's try first.","tool_calls":[{"name":"call_mcp_tool","args":{"Arguments":{"channel_id":"https://www.youtube.com/@Brainosophic"},"ServerName":"nexlev","ToolName":"check_channel_monetization","toolAction":"Testing NexLev connection","toolSummary":"Brainosophy monetization"}}]}
